      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# OptiCell — BBBC039 validation on Google Colab\n",
        "\n",
        "**Measured metrics only.** Runs classical threshold and optional Cellpose on U2OS nuclei (BBBC039).\n",
        "\n",
        "**Setup:** Runtime → Change runtime type → **T4 GPU** (or any GPU).\n",
        "\n",
        "Repo: [Virelion-OptiCell](https://github.com/Virelion-Biotech/Virelion-OptiCell)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Install dependencies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import torch\n",
        "print('CUDA available:', torch.cuda.is_available())\n",
        "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
        "    print('GPU:', torch.cuda.get_device_name(0))\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('WARNING: no GPU — Cellpose will be slow. Enable GPU runtime.')"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "!pip -q install opencv-python-headless tifffile scipy pandas packaging cellpose\n",
        "print('deps ok')"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Clone OptiCell + download BBBC039"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import os\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "WORK = Path('/content/Virelion-OptiCell')\n",
        "if not (WORK / 'qc_pipeline.py').exists():\n",
        "    !git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/Virelion-Biotech/Virelion-OptiCell.git {WORK}\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print('repo already present')\n",
        "\n",
        "%cd {WORK}\n",
        "!pip -q install -e .\n",
        "print('cwd:', os.getcwd())"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import urllib.request, zipfile\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "DATA = Path('data/bbbc039')\n",
        "RAW = DATA / 'raw'\n",
        "IMG_DIR = DATA / 'images'\n",
        "MSK_DIR = DATA / 'masks'\n",
        "RAW.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "urls = {\n",
        "    'images.zip': 'https://data.broadinstitute.org/bbbc/BBBC039/images.zip',\n",
        "    'masks.zip': 'https://data.broadinstitute.org/bbbc/BBBC039/masks.zip',\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "for name, url in urls.items():\n",
        "    dest = RAW / name\n",
        "    if dest.exists() and dest.stat().st_size > 0:\n",
        "        print(f'skip download {name}')\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "    print(f'downloading {name} ...')\n",
        "    urllib.request.urlretrieve(url, dest)\n",
        "    print(f'  -> {dest.stat().st_size/1e6:.1f} MB')\n",
        "\n",
        "for zname, out in [('images.zip', IMG_DIR), ('masks.zip', MSK_DIR)]:\n",
        "    marker = out / '.extracted'\n",
        "    if marker.exists():\n",
        "        print(f'skip extract {zname}')\n",
        "        continue\n",
        "    out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    print(f'extracting {zname} ...')\n",
        "    with zipfile.ZipFile(RAW / zname) as zf:\n",
        "        zf.extractall(out)\n",
        "    marker.write_text('ok')\n",
        "print('BBBC039 ready')"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Config — change these"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "MAX_IMAGES = 50          # pilot; use 200 for full BBBC039\n",
        "RUN_THRESHOLD = True\n",
        "RUN_CELLPOSE = True      # needs GPU for reasonable speed\n",
        "CELLPOSE_MODEL = 'cpsam' # Cellpose 4 default SAM model\n",
        "USE_GPU = True           # set False only if no GPU runtime"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Run validation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import sys\n",
        "sys.path.insert(0, str(WORK))\n",
        "\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "def run_backend(backend: str, gpu: bool = False):\n",
        "    cmd = [\n",
        "        sys.executable, 'scripts/run_bbbc039_validation.py',\n",
        "        '--max-images', str(MAX_IMAGES),\n",
        "        '--backend', backend,\n",
        "        '--skip-download',\n",
        "        '--out-dir', 'outputs/bbbc039_validation',\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    if backend == 'cellpose':\n",
        "        cmd += ['--cellpose-model', CELLPOSE_MODEL]\n",
        "        if gpu:\n",
        "            cmd.append('--gpu')\n",
        "    print('>>>', ' '.join(cmd))\n",
        "    import subprocess\n",
        "    r = subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=str(WORK))\n",
        "    if r.returncode != 0:\n",
        "        raise SystemExit(f'{backend} failed with code {r.returncode}')\n",
        "\n",
        "if RUN_THRESHOLD:\n",
        "    run_backend('threshold')\n",
        "\n",
        "if RUN_CELLPOSE:\n",
        "    run_backend('cellpose', gpu=USE_GPU)"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Show measured summaries"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import json\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "out = Path('outputs/bbbc039_validation')\n",
        "files = sorted(out.glob('bbbc039_*_n*.json'))\n",
        "if not files:\n",
        "    print('No result JSON yet')\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    for f in files:\n",
        "        data = json.loads(f.read_text())\n",
        "        s = data['summary']\n",
        "        print('=' * 60)\n",
        "        print(f"File: {f.name}")\n",
        "        print(f"backend={data.get('backend')}  n={data.get('n_scored')}  gpu={data.get('gpu')}")\n",
        "        print(f"  IoU:   {s.get('iou', s.get('pixel_iou_mean')):.4f}")\n",
        "        print(f"  Dice:  {s.get('dice', s.get('pixel_dice_mean')):.4f}")\n",
        "        print(f"  F1:    {s.get('f1', s.get('instance_f1_mean')):.4f}")\n",
        "        print(f"  |count err| mean: {s.get('absolute_count_error_mean', s.get('absolute_count_error')):.2f}")\n",
        "        print(f"  rel count err:    {s.get('relative_count_error_mean', s.get('relative_count_error'))}")\n",
        "    print('=' * 60)\n",
        "    print('These numbers are measured only — not fabricated.')"
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Download results to your machine\n",
        "\n",
        "Left sidebar → folder icon → `Virelion-OptiCell/outputs/bbbc039_validation/` → download JSON/CSV.\n",
        "Or run:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
